tive factor of 2 for both local algorithms [RV17] and low-degree algorithms [Wei22]. In our work
we focus on low-degree algorithms (see §1.2 for an overview of the framework).
    Moving beyond graphs to hypergraphs, we are interested in the sparse regime, i.e., p = d/ n−1
