Step 0 is decisive: there is no admissible family here. Below the threshold, Sections 3.1 and 4.2 explicitly produce witnesses algorithmically (the multipartite one is degree 1), so H fails; above the threshold, the paper’s low-degree impossibility applies to unconditioned random instances, but no construction retains an answer certificate. Planting repairs G only by leaving the theorem’s distribution. I’m recording that rejection rather than fabricating gates for an unsupported planted model.
