The paper’s hardness results apply to unconditioned Erdős–Rényi hypergraphs. Planting an independent set changes that distribution, so the low-degree lower bounds no longer apply. Conversely, the paper’s certificate-producing regimes use explicit local/random-greedy algorithms—and a degree-1 algorithm for the multipartite case—so they fail H’s discriminating test. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2404.03842v3)

The complete rationale is recorded in [REJECTED.md](/Users/jang-wongi/Desktop/WG/PI_LAB/arxiv-gv-problems/results/2404.03842/REJECTED.md). It documents the exact regimes, planting mismatch, Track B analysis, and alternative formulations considered.
